g accusations from two of  his own sons  global's kevin hirschfield joins me now  from nygard's hometown of winnipeg kevin  what can you tell us well robin the  allegations continue to mount against  winnipeg fashion mogul peter nygaard who  is facing another lawsuit  his latest accusers two of his sons  in the latest lawsuit the sons allege  their father ordered his girlfriend who  the suit claims is a full-time sex  worker  to statutorily rape them 14 years apart  when they were teenagers  the first complainant alleges nygard's  son was flown from california  to nightguard's winnipeg home in 2018 at  14 years old  where nygard orchestrated the alleged  rape to quote  make a man out of him according to the  court documents  but the accusations state this wasn't  the first time nygaard had arranged the  alleged rape of one of his sons  in 2004 he's accused of instructing the  same woman to have sex with his other  son  who was allegedly 15 at the time at a  beachfront property in the bahamas  now one of nygard's lawyers jay prober  says his client denies the allegations  peter nygard believes this is part of  the continued  conspiracy against him and part of the  continued  publicity campaign against him nygard  has already been accused of sexual  assault by 57 women in a separate class  action lawsuit  none of the accusations in either  lawsuit have been proven in court  and nygard claims it is a conspiracy and  publicity campaign  against him robin kevin hirschfield in  winnipeg  still ahead in a time when it's  important to stay in why are airlines  urging canadians  to fly out  you're watching global national  [Music]  the canada u.s border remains closed to  all non-essential travel  until at least september 21st but some  travelers have been taking advantage of  a loophole that allows them to fly  back and forth and as shawn o'shea  reports one canadian airline is even  promoting this kind of travel at  toronto's pearson international known as  canada's busiest  airport passenger terminals haven't been  crowded for five months  many medical experts say that's a good  thing we're in the middle of a pandemic  we need to keep that border closed  until you know it's safe to open and  right now it's not safe to open  and while the land border to the united  states is restricted to all but  essential travel  you can legally fly to the united states  for leisure travel if you like  they even tell you how to do it are you  eager to reunite with friends and  relatives in the u.s  did you know that canadians are  permitted to travel by  air to and from the us for leisure or  business  probably should be some social  responsibility here is in the sense that  the borders closed for non-essential  travel but not  being advertising non-essential travel  the government of canada still advises  against all non-essential travel outside  the country  and where the u.s is concerned some  experts say caution is especially  important  i mean going to an area with lots of  community transmission  of kova 19 where you're going to be in  contact with other people  i would advise against that air canada  says it's offering essential services  and allowing families to reunite the  company also told global news in a  statement that it follows  all federal rules and has put in place  industry-leading bio safety measures  to protect customers and employees the  airline industry association wants the  government to consider allowing more  travel  to countries where the virus is under  control jill murphy is traveling to  boston to visit her ailing grandmother  people don't have to go then there's  nothing there's no reason to go to a  place that  doesn't have the greatest of safety  recommendations right now she says  she'd rather stay home and can't  understand why anyone would plan a  pleasure trip south  during a pandemic sean o'shea global  news toronto  up next canadian football is officially  hunted by the pandemic  hopes have been dashed for c